{
  "name": "04 - Notifications / Error Trigger",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "node-0021",
      "name": "Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        240,
        -140
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Error Trigger\n\nSingle Responsibility: the instance-wide safety net. Every other workflow already calls System Error explicitly on its designed failure branches (HTTP call fails after retries, health check returns non-2xx, etc.) — this one catches everything those branches don't: a node throwing an unhandled exception, a malformed trigger payload, a timeout, anything that crashes a workflow before it ever reaches its own error handling.\n\nSetup (one-time, per workflow, after import): open each workflow → Settings (gear icon) → Error Workflow → select \"04 - Notifications / Error Trigger\". Do this for every workflow in 01-intake, 02-processing, 03-budgetflow-api-client, and 06-scheduling-orchestration. This workflow's own trigger node only fires when referenced this way — it does nothing if just left inactive and unreferenced.\n\nDoes not need activating like a normal workflow — n8n runs error workflows regardless of their own active state.",
        "height": 400,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "node-0020",
      "name": "On Any Workflow Error",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.errorTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        240,
        340
      ],
      "parameters": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "node-0022",
      "name": "Format Error",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        520,
        340
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "manual",
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "node-0023",
              "name": "workflow",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.workflow.name }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "node-0024",
              "name": "message",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ ($json.execution.error && $json.execution.error.message) || 'Unhandled error' }}{{ $json.execution.lastNodeExecuted ? (' (node: ' + $json.execution.lastNodeExecuted + ')') : '' }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "node-0025",
              "name": "statusCode",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "node-0026",
              "name": "context",
              "type": "object",
              "value": "={{ { executionId: $json.execution.id, executionUrl: $json.execution.url, mode: $json.execution.mode, retryOf: $json.execution.retryOf || null } }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "node-0027",
      "name": "Notify Ops",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.executeWorkflow",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        800,
        340
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "source": "database",
        "workflowId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "SELECT_AFTER_IMPORT:04 - Notifications / System Error",
          "cachedResultName": "04 - Notifications / System Error"
        },
        "workflowInputs": {
          "mappingMode": "autoMapInputData",
          "value": {}
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "notesInFlow": true,
      "notes": "After importing, point this at \"04 - Notifications / System Error\" (n8n assigns IDs on import)."
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "On Any Workflow Error": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Format Error",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Format Error": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Notify Ops",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    }
  },
  "active": false,
  "settings": {
    "executionOrder": "v1",
    "saveManualExecutions": true
  },
  "tags": []
}
